---
layout: null
permalink: /sitemap.xml
---
{%- comment -%}
  hreflang lives here and only here. Google documents the sitemap form as
  equivalent to the head tags, and one list cannot disagree with another.

  RECIPROCITY IS BY CONSTRUCTION, which is the whole reason the family is
  derived from the path rather than declared per page. Google's rule is blunt:
  if two pages do not both point at each other the annotations are ignored,
  silently, with nothing in a Jekyll build or a Pages build status able to see
  it. Every member of a family computes the identical list, itself included, so
  an asymmetric annotation is unsayable here. The anti-pattern is a per-page
  list of translations: six hand-maintained links at three languages and ninety
  at ten, any one of which voids the cluster.

  `layout: null` in front matter beats the `layout: doc` default, which is what
  keeps HTML off an XML file. `absolute_url` and `xml_escape` are core Jekyll
  filters, not plugin-provided, so they survive Pages' safe mode; they need the
  `url` and `baseurl` that _config.yml now sets.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
        xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
{%- for p in site.pages -%}
{%- unless p.url contains '.xml' or p.url contains '.txt' %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ p.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
{%- assign stem = p.path -%}
{%- for l in site.languages -%}
  {%- if l.code == p.lang and l.dir != "" -%}
    {%- assign under = l.dir | append: "/" -%}
    {%- assign stem = p.path | remove_first: under -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign family = 0 -%}
{%- for l in site.languages -%}
  {%- if l.dir == "" -%}{%- assign want = stem -%}
  {%- else -%}{%- assign want = l.dir | append: "/" | append: stem -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign v = site.pages | where: "path", want | first -%}
  {%- if v -%}{%- assign family = family | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if family > 1 -%}
{%- for l in site.languages -%}
  {%- if l.dir == "" -%}{%- assign want = stem -%}
  {%- else -%}{%- assign want = l.dir | append: "/" | append: stem -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign v = site.pages | where: "path", want | first -%}
  {%- if v %}
    <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ l.code }}" href="{{ v.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}"/>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign x = site.pages | where: "path", stem | first -%}
{%- if x %}
    <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ x.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}"/>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif %}
  </url>
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
